      "text": "Composition-Diamond Lemma for Modules ∗ — In this paper we give some relationships among the Gr¨ obner-Shirsh ov bases in free associative algebras, free left modules and “double-free” le ft modules\n\n**Composition-Diamond Lemma for Modules ∗**\n\n*Yuqun Chen, Yongshan Chen and Chanyan Zhong*\n\n16 pp, 6 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this paper we give some relationships among the Gr¨ obner-Shirsh ov bases in free associative algebras, free left modules and “double-free” le ft modules (free modules over a free algebra). We give the Chibrikov’s Composition-Diamond lem ma for modules and show that Kang-Lee’s Composition-Diamond lemma follows from th is lemma. As applications, we also deal with highest weight module over the Lie algeb ra sl2, Verma module over a Kac-Moody algebra, Verma module over Lie algebra of c oeﬃcients of a free conformal algebra and the universal enveloping module for a Sabinin algebra.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; Composition-Diamond lemma for left ideals of a; Highest weight modules over sl2; Verma module over Kac-Moody algebras; Universal enveloping module for a Sabinin alge\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 2.6: Let (S, T ) be a pair of subsets of monic elements in k⟨X⟩, let\n- Theorem 3.4: Let X, Y be well ordered sets, < a monomial order on X ∗, ≺ the order\n- Theorem 6.4: Let the notions be as above. Then a k-basis of V consists of elements\n- Theorem 7.3: Let I be as above. Then I is the Gr¨ obner-Shirshov basis in mod⟨X⟩k⟨X⟩.\n- Theorem 7.4: Let {ai|i ∈ Λ } be a totally ordered basis of\n- Corollary 5.2: R = {T X∗(v), N+(v), h (v) − Λ( h)v} is a Gr¨ obner-Shirshov basis for the",
